  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EEffective self-care can help people with heart failure recognise deterioration early and feel more confident managing their condition. Nurses can support this by tailoring education to the person\u0027s health literacy, language, culture, cognition and home supports.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EKey Teaching Points\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EDaily weights:\u003C/strong\u003E Weigh each morning after using the toilet and before breakfast, using the same scales and similar clothing. Record the result and report a gain of more than 2 kg over 2 to 3 days, or as advised by the treating team.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ESymptoms:\u003C/strong\u003E Monitor breathlessness, swelling, fatigue, dizziness, sleep changes and the number of pillows needed at night.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EMedicines:\u003C/strong\u003E Explain the purpose of each medicine and common side effects. Encourage patients to use reminders, keep an up-to-date list and check with a pharmacist or doctor before taking NSAIDs or new supplements.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EDiet and fluids:\u003C/strong\u003E Provide individualised sodium and fluid advice, as restrictions are not appropriate for everyone. Remind patients not to use potassium-based salt substitutes unless advised.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EActivity:\u003C/strong\u003E Encourage appropriate regular activity and offer referral to cardiac rehabilitation where available.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ELifestyle and wellbeing:\u003C/strong\u003E Support smoking cessation, safe alcohol use and vaccinations. Screen for low mood, anxiety, poor sleep and social isolation.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EChecking Understanding\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe teach-back method can confirm understanding. For example, ask, \u0022What would you do if your weight rose by 2 kg in two days?\u0022 A written action plan should explain what is normal for the person, when to contact the care team and when to call 000.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhen to Seek Emergency Help\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EPatients should seek emergency help for severe breathlessness, chest pain, fainting or sudden confusion. Include carers and family members where appropriate, and arrange follow-up contact after discharge or medication changes.\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </bodyContent>
